<title>FRANCE: Sally Ferries cuts one Dunkerque-Ramsgate ferry.</title>
<headline>Sally Ferries cuts one Dunkerque-Ramsgate ferry.</headline>
<dateline>LILLE, France 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish shipping firm Sally Ferries said on Wednesday it would remove one of its two ferries plying the Dunkerque-Ramsgate route, the Sally Sky, eliminating 152 jobs.</p>
<p>The Sally Sky can carry 1,200 passengers and 450 cars. The larger ferry on the route, the Sally Star, will reduce the number of daily round trips to three from five, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Sally Ferries, the only ferry company serving Dunkerque, has been feeling pressure in recent months from competition from Channel Tunnel operator Eurotunnel. frs/cct</p>
</text>
